############# About the Project ############

## Project Overview

The **Autonomous Obstacle Avoiding Robot** is a small autonomous robotic vehicle developed using an Arduino UNO, ultrasonic sensor, IR sensors, L298N motor driver, and gear motors.

The main purpose of the project is to enable the robot to move through a given path while detecting obstacles and automatically changing its direction without continuous human control.

The robot continuously monitors its surroundings using sensors. When an obstacle is detected in front of it, the Arduino processes the sensor inputs and determines a suitable direction to avoid the obstacle. The L298N motor driver then controls the motors according to the decision made by the Arduino.

This project demonstrates the basic principles of **autonomous navigation, sensor-based decision making, motor control, and embedded systems**.


## Problem Statement

A manually controlled robotic vehicle requires continuous human input to navigate and avoid obstacles.

The objective of this project is to develop a robotic vehicle that can **detect obstacles, make basic navigation decisions, and continue moving autonomously**.



## Objective

The main objectives of this project are:

- To develop an autonomous robotic vehicle.
- To detect obstacles in real time.
- To determine a suitable direction when an obstacle is encountered.
- To control the robot's movement automatically.
- To gain practical experience in robotics and embedded systems.



